{% doc %}
  Style With Card Mobile

  Renders a single mobile "Style With" card on the PDP: a full-bleed 160×240
  image tile with an overlaid quick-add icon, no title/price.

  @param {product} card_product - Product object (required)

  @example
  {% render 'style-with-card-mobile', card_product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign card_product = card_product | default: blank

  unless card_product != blank
    break
  endunless
-%}

<div class="style-with-card-mobile relative h-[240px] w-[160px] shrink-0 bg-surface-soft" data-style-with-card-mobile>
  <a href="{{ card_product.url }}" class="absolute inset-0">
    {%- if card_product.featured_image != blank -%}
      <img
        src="{{ card_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 320 }}"
        srcset="{{ card_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 }} 1x, {{ card_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 320 }} 2x"
        sizes="160px"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="{{ card_product.title | escape }}"
        width="160"
        height="240"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      >
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center text-muted">
        {%- render 'icon-cart', size: 32 -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </a>

  {%- comment -%}
    No explicit z-index: position:absolute alone already paints this above the
    card's image (it comes after it in DOM order), and adding one here would
    trap quick-add-atc's fixed scrim/panel inside a local stacking context,
    capping their effective priority instead of letting them compete at the
    root level against sibling cards in the row (see the same reasoning in
    product-card.liquid's image_cluster_wrapper_class comment).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="absolute bottom-[10px] right-[16px]">
    {%- render 'quick-add-atc',
      product: card_product,
      button_class: 'bg-ink-20 text-white',
      compact_pad_class: 'h-6 w-6'
    -%}
  </div>
</div>
